      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "03faec09-d110-5bb2-bba6-a745c30e3eba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rolls Gracie, Royler Gracie, Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado, Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti, Rodrigo Medeiros, Fernando \"Magrao\" Gurgel, Saulo Ribeiro, Hélio Gracie\n- Organizations: Gracie Humaitá\n- Places: Rio de Janeiro, San Diego, Brazil\n- Roles: martial artists, teachers, students, competitors\n- Topics: Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu, Judo, World Jiu-Jitsu Championship\n\nFacts:\n- Rolls Gracie was a Brazilian martial artist who lived from 1951 to 1982.\n- Rolls Gracie taught Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Royler Gracie, Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado, and Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti.\n- Royler Gracie ran the Gracie Humaitá school in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil for many years under his father Hélio Gracie's direction.\n- Royler Gracie currently lives in San Diego.\n- Rodrigo Medeiros received his black belt from Romero \"Jacaré\" Cavalcanti, who was a student of Rolls Gracie.\n- Rodrigo Medeiros also trained under Fernando \"Magrao\" Gurgel.\n- Rodrigo Medeiros is one of a select group of Jiu-Jitsu competitors to have won the World Jiu-Jitsu Championship openweight title twice.\n- After earning a black belt in Judo, Saulo Ribeiro began training in Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu in Rio de Janeiro under Royler Gracie at Gracie Humaitá.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "59e01f94-a8cb-5145-9edc-b052728340d4",
        "text": "Page: Rolls Gracie. Sentence: Rolls Gracie ([ˈɡɾejsi] 1951–1982) was a Brazilian martial artist.\nPage: Rolls Gracie. Sentence: He was teacher of Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Royler Gracie, Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado and Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti.\nPage: Royler Gracie. Sentence: He ran the Gracie Humaitá school in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil for many years under his father Helio's direction, but currently lives in San Diego.\nPage: Rodrigo Medeiros. Sentence: He received his black belt from Rolls Gracie student, Romero \"Jacaré\" Cavalcanti, he also trained under Fernando 'Magrao' Gurgel and is one of a select group of Jiu-Jitsu competitors to have won the prestigious World Jiu-Jitsu Championship openweight titles twice.\nPage: Saulo Ribeiro. Sentence: After earning a black belt in Judo, he began his training of Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu in Rio de Janeiro under Royler Gracie, the son of Hélio Gracie, at the famous Gracie Humaitá.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
